# Wall-shadow geometry capture. Run twice - once with the pre-fix shaders in the
# install, once with the fixed ones - against the SAME save and the SAME scene.
# Shaders are compiled at runtime from datadir (load_lighting_shader_source), so
# swapping the .hlsl files between runs needs no rebuild and changes nothing
# else about the binary.
#
# Night is mandatory: sprite.frag resolves combined = max(tint.rgb, gpu_total),
# so in daylight the CPU lightmap tint dominates and GPU shadowing is invisible.
launch --dont-debugmsg
waitlog "opened document data/gui/mainmenu.rml" timeout=240000
focus
key "o"
wait 800
key "{ENTER}"
wait 1500
key "h"
wait 3000
key "{ENTER}"
wait 8000
key "{SPACE}"
wait 1500
key "{SPACE}"
wait 1500
key "{SPACE}"
wait 1500
key "{SPACE}"
waitlog "opened document .*sidebar_hud.rml" timeout=300000
wait 6000
key "!"
wait 1500

# ---- night ----
key "{ESC}"
wait 1800
key "c"
wait 2000
key "m"
wait 1800
key "t"
wait 2000
key "h"
wait 1500
key "{BACKSPACE}"
wait 300
key "{BACKSPACE}"
wait 300
key "1"
wait 500
key "{ENTER}"
wait 1500
key "{ESC}"
wait 1200
key "{ESC}"
wait 1200
key "{ESC}"
wait 3000

# ---- zoom in so the shadow edge spans enough pixels to measure ----
# Zoom must be DETERMINISTIC or the A/B compares two different cameras. A bare
# run of 'z' presses is not: a dropped keypress silently leaves a different zoom
# level, which shifts the whole frame and makes every luma/gradient comparison
# meaningless (it cost a full round of bogus "contrast collapse" numbers).
# Saturate against the zoom-out clamp first, then step in a fixed count, so the
# final level is the same even if individual presses are eaten.
# NB: '{Z*10}' would NOT work here - the named-key path lowercases the token
# (VkKeyScanW(main.lower())) and would send zoom-IN ten times. Literal text is
# injected as Unicode and preserves case, so 'Z' really is zoom-out.
# Each press needs its own settle: sent back to back, most are dropped, and the
# run silently ends on a different zoom level. That is not cosmetic - measured
# across four captures, zoom bistability moved whole-frame mean luma by 19.7
# (tile pitch 8.02px vs 42.86px) and completely swamped the shader effect being
# tested. Saturate against the zoom-out clamp with spaced presses, then step in
# a fixed count. tools/shadow_zoom_check.py verifies the resulting tile pitch.
key "Z"
wait 350
key "Z"
wait 350
key "Z"
wait 350
key "Z"
wait 350
key "Z"
wait 350
key "Z"
wait 350
key "Z"
wait 350
key "Z"
wait 350
key "Z"
wait 350
key "Z"
wait 350
key "Z"
wait 350
key "Z"
wait 1500
# Wide view: zoom-out saturation only. This is the regime where the emitter
# shadow path measurably reaches the screen (scene-1 showed 3.48%).

# ---- build the wall + single light ----
key "{ESC}"
wait 1800
key "c"
wait 2000
key "l"
wait 3000
key "{ENTER}"
wait 2500
key "require(\"lib.shadowtest\")"
wait 2000
key "{CTRL+S}"
wait 6000
key "{ESC}"
wait 5000
shot shadow
wait 2500
shot shadow_again
